# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Ryan Liu et al. (2026). From Evaluation to Design: Using Potential Energy Surface Smoothness Metrics to Guide Machine Learning Interatomic Potential Architectures.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2602.04861  arXiv:2602.04861v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2602.04861v2 (sha256 695944b622bcd5d2...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 274 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/liu2026evaluation.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the MinDScAIP attention-based MLIP introduced here,
# trained on SPICE (MACE-OFF split) in the ablations of Table 2 (smoothness
# designs, prediction heads, model sizes) with the MACE and GemNet-T
# baselines, its per-subset SPICE test errors (Table 4), the MPtrj-trained
# MinDScAIP-60M on Matbench Discovery (Table 5) and the inference
# throughput benchmark (Table 6). The BSCT force-smoothness deviation (FSD),
# NVE energy drift, F1, kappa_SRME and RMSD are not error metrics of the
# schema and are not encoded; other models' Table 4 and Table 5 values are
# quoted from the literature and leaderboard and are not encoded.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
