###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Inference throughput (Table 6, one A100 80 GB, diamond): MinDScAIP-60M
# 1.15 to 0.09 million steps per day from 216 to 2,744 atoms, MACE-MP-16M
# 1.49 to 0.15, eSEN-30M-OAM 0.09 at 216 atoms and out of memory above;
# per-atom times are 86,400 s / (steps per day x atoms). FSD on BSCT takes
# about 40 minutes on one A6000 GPU against about 40 hours for the MD
# stability test. No training times are given.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - MinDScAIP is a new registry method (origin this paper); the paper presents it as a neutral testbed similar to a Swin Transformer and states no derivation from a registry method. The 'Gradient Diff-kNN' and 'Large' rows of Table 2 are the same model (identical values) and are encoded once.
# - Appendix F says the SPICE results of Table 4 come from the MPtrj-trained Smear. & Temp. model, while Table 4 and Table 7 describe a SPICE-trained Smear. & Temp. 60M model; the Table 4 values are attached to the SPICE Smear. & Temp. run.
# - The provenance of the MACE Large (4.7M) and GemNet-T SPICE baselines (trained here or taken from earlier work) is not stated. The MACE, EScAIP and eSEN columns of Table 4 and the other models of Table 5 are literature or leaderboard values and are not encoded.
# - MACE-MP-16M and eSEN-30M-OAM are named without further identification and are paper-local runs. FSD, NVE energy drift, max kinetic-temperature jumps, F1, kappa_SRME and RMSD (Tables 1-3, 5) are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/liu2026evaluation.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

